# Incident agent — architecture rules

Follow `docs/CODING_PRINCIPLES.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## Layers (do not mix)

- `contracts/` — types only (`IncidentState`, etc.)
- Business (`nodes/`, `remediation/`, `validation/`) — domain decisions; no LLM, no live I/O
- Orchestration (`graph.py`, `pipeline.py`, `routing.py`) — sequencing / replan only
- `providers/` — Observation / Metrics / Execution / Memory / LLM adapters
- `llm/` — advisory suggestion clients + ingestion; never routing, approval, or execution
- Later: `prompts/`, `tools/` — do not dump those into business nodes

## Structure

- Flat over deep; max 3–4 levels under `src/incident_agent/`
- No `utils/`, `helpers/`, `misc/`, or cryptic names
- Runtime data (`logs`, `memory`, `state`, artifacts) only under `runtime/`, `data/`, or `artifacts/` — never under `src/`

## When editing

- Prefer small, named functions (≈40 lines; refactor before ≈60)
- Delete dead code you replace
- Keep Stage-0 paths deterministic and testable without API keys/clusters
- Match existing patterns; update tests for behavior changes
